@startuml
' Source of truth for 02-write-flow.png -- see ../README.md to regenerate.
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam shadowing false
autonumber
title Write (encrypt) flow

participant "SQL client" as C
participant "FE\n(StarRocks)" as FE
participant "Iceberg lib\n(in the FE process)" as ICE
participant "BE" as BE
participant "Object store" as OBJ
participant "KMS" as KMS
participant "Iceberg catalog" as CAT

C -> FE : INSERT / DELETE / UPDATE / MERGE\non an encryption-enabled iceberg table
note over FE
  A table is encrypted iff it declares encryption.key-id.
  IcebergEncryption.writeSignalOrNull reads that property --
  NOT the manager's type -- because the commit path reads the
  same property; deciding it two different ways would encrypt
  a file whose commit records no key.
  Refused here if the table declares encryption but the catalog
  supplied a PlaintextEncryptionManager.
end note
note over FE
  All three sinks derive the signal from that one place:
  IcebergTableSink (INSERT), IcebergDeleteSink (DELETE) and
  IcebergRowDeltaSink (UPDATE / MERGE), so a position-delete
  file is encrypted exactly like a data file.
end note

== Data file (and position-delete file) ==
FE -> BE : sink encryption info -- algorithm + DEK length, NO key
note over FE
  Algorithm is always AES_GCM_V1. Iceberg has no cipher table
  property, and GCM is the only PME mode that authenticates page
  DATA -- AES_GCM_CTR_V1 would leave pages unauthenticated.
end note
note over BE
  generate a fresh per-file DEK with RAND_bytes
  (length validated in {16,24,32}) plus a 16-byte AAD prefix
end note
BE -> OBJ : write PME-encrypted Parquet\nencrypted footer, single footer key, no per-column keys
BE --> FE : return PLAINTEXT file_dek and aad_prefix
note over BE : zeroize the DEK (OPENSSL_cleanse) on writer destroy

== Commit ==
note over FE
  key_metadata = StandardKeyMetadata(DEK, aad_prefix), applied to
  data files AND position-delete files alike.
  -- the data key IN THE CLEAR. Safe only because the
  manifest carrying it is encrypted below.
  An encrypted table whose file arrives with NO key, or a key of
  the wrong length, is refused rather than committed.
end note
FE -> ICE : commit data file + key_metadata
note over ICE : generate manifest key + AAD prefix\n(driver side, secure RNG)
ICE -> OBJ : write manifest as AES-GCM stream (AGS1)\ncarrying each data file's key_metadata
ICE -> OBJ : write manifest list as AES-GCM stream (AGS1)\ncarrying each manifest's key, prefix, length
note over ICE
  pack the manifest-list key + prefix + length into a key
  metadata object and encrypt it with a KEK, using the KEK
  creation timestamp as the AES-GCM AAD
end note
ICE -> KMS : wrap the KEK with the table master key
KMS --> ICE : wrapped KEK
ICE -> CAT : metadata.json (NOT encrypted):\nencryption-keys = [wrapped KEK, encrypted ML key metadata]\nsnapshot.key-id = KEK_ID
note over KMS : one KMS call per KEK, not per file
@enduml
